    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "62a39d8a_918192b8",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_protocol.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 372,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003000
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-07-04T20:37:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What scenario is that? Isn\u0027t it bad to end up in that situation? If EC thinks that TCPC is not in low power mode when it actually is, it could make an i2c transaction to put TCPC into low power mode thus resulting in TCPC actually waking up from LPM. If the rare scenario is repeatable, then we could end up in an indefinite loop.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 370,
        "startChar": 43,
        "endLine": 372,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "859f09bb4fdd84de89bf39a8f03ca54d9880d00b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2b937c2d_c69a559e",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_protocol.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 373,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002124
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-07-03T21:54:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This path is still in the hook task. As such the real state of things can be incorrect.",
      "revId": "859f09bb4fdd84de89bf39a8f03ca54d9880d00b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "201e8b39_701c0158",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_protocol.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 375,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003000
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-07-04T20:37:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ideally, we would want these two to be atomic. Once the deferred function sets this flag, there is no guarantee that it will continue running to put TCPC into low power mode. There could be another task scheduled which starts talking to the TCPC at this point.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 374,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 375,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "859f09bb4fdd84de89bf39a8f03ca54d9880d00b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3f3cad1f_e8a4f332",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_protocol.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 382,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003000
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-07-04T20:37:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "One of the assumptions is that all accesses to TCPC are going through the standard tcpc_* functions. I think there are some functions in anx e.g. anx7447_reg_read/write which make I2C transaction directly without calling into tcpc_read/write.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 382,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 382,
        "endChar": 23
      },
      "revId": "859f09bb4fdd84de89bf39a8f03ca54d9880d00b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "02baedc1_44bc2d11",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_protocol.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 415,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003000
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-07-04T20:37:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Scott had pointed out this issue some time back. When coming out of low power mode, we should be making a throwaway transaction to ensure that we actually take the TCPC out of low power mode. Should we be taking care of that here?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 415,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 415,
        "endChar": 14
      },
      "revId": "859f09bb4fdd84de89bf39a8f03ca54d9880d00b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2c64fbf1_44db48d5",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_protocol.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 3587,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002124
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-07-03T21:54:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If there\u0027s an ordering requirement here I think a small comment would help for future readability and context.",
      "revId": "859f09bb4fdd84de89bf39a8f03ca54d9880d00b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
